## Tags & Visibility

**Tags** are movable pointers. `bundles tag` advances a tag to an exact checksum — the reference **must** be the `@sha256:…` form (resolve a tag to its checksum first with `bundles get`/`tags`).
```
beam_exec("bundles tag checkout-stack@sha256:abc123… stable -q")
```
{{ if commands["bundles tag"] }}{{ if (array.size commands["bundles tag"].arguments) > 0 }}
#### `beam bundles tag` arguments
| Argument | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
{{ for arg in commands["bundles tag"].arguments }}| `{{ arg.name }}` | {{ arg.type }} | {{ arg.description }} |
{{ end }}{{ end }}{{ if (array.size commands["bundles tag"].options) > 0 }}
#### `beam bundles tag` options
| Option | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
{{ for opt in commands["bundles tag"].options }}| `{{ opt.name }}` | {{ opt.type }} | {{ opt.description }} |
{{ end }}{{ end }}{{ end }}

**ACL scope** controls who may *reference* a checksum. The three tiers are **supersets**, not lists of realms, and you can only ever **widen**:
- `realm` — only the current realm (`<cid>.<pid>`). This is the default at publish time.
- `org` — every realm in your customer (`<cid>`).
- `public` — every realm in every customer (`*`).

`bundles acl` accepts a bare name or `@tag` (it resolves to the checksum) as well as an exact `@sha256:…`. Widening is **admin-gated server-side** — a non-admin token is rejected even though the CLI accepts the argument.
```
beam_exec("bundles acl checkout-stack@sha256:abc123… --scope org -q")
```
{{ if commands["bundles acl"] }}{{ if (array.size commands["bundles acl"].arguments) > 0 }}
#### `beam bundles acl` arguments
